Takahashi-san ga shouten shimashita yo!

Though I've been playing NetHack for years, I've only ascended three
times, all in the past month, so please indulge me because I never
actually did my YAFAP.  The first two were a Valkyrie and a Monk,
respectively, but last night, I ascended a 5-day old Samurai.

See, I'm in the middle of playing a Wizard who's doing generally fine
but having little luck with the RNG (no stores or altars on the top 25
levels of the main dungeon, nothing more exciting than tin openers for
sale in minetown, etc.), so to take a break from that rather mediocre
game, I started a new one with Takahashi the Samurai.

Takahashi was lucky from the start: her pet stole speed boots from a
store on DL2 (or maybe DL5), she found a [CoMR and "AoR in the mines
early on, and got silver dragon scale mail from a throne.  She was
two-weaponing +7 Snickersnee (sacrifice) and a +6 wazakashi in the
early game and +6 Frost Brand (magic lamp) with a +6 katana (later, a
+7 silver saber) by the time she started the Quest.  She didn't even
bother trying out her Tsurugi.  I guess once you go two-weapon, you
never go back!

With the /WoW from the castle, she got a blessed scroll of genocide
and a magic marker.  I couldn't resist genociding "h" and "L", but I
did resist the temptation to use her two wands of polymorph for any
monkey business.  After she reached Juiblex' swamp without finding a
ring of levitation, I wished for one of those, too.

Anyway, the *real* luck came in the endgame.  She had two wands of
death---one from Ludios and one from Orcus---and she killed Rodney
with two zaps from one of those.  I think she was level 18 at the time
with around 325 HP and an AC of -35 or so.

In a departure from my previous attempts, I decided to try to ascend
without a ring of conflict (though I had a wish in reserve just in
case).  Moloch's Sanctum was an honest if relatively easy fight, and
two-weaponing graveyards with FB and a silver saber is highly
recommended.  Anyway, after a pause in the altar room to do a little
HP-related alchemy and AC-related finishing touches, I steeled myself
for a difficult, lawful ascension with the Amulet.

However, on the trip up to the Valley, all 23 staircases of it, a
"mysterious force" surrounded little Takahashi *TWICE*.  That's right,
*TWICE*.  And that was it.  She literally ran into a cockatrice on
DL45, and had a corpse in hand for her next encounter with Rodney.
She refreshed the corpse in a DL19 nest I'd been saving (and the old
corpse actually rotted away the turn before she picked up the fresh
one) and stoned Rodney twice more before the final stoning on the
Plane of Earth.

The Plane of Air was truly difficult.  I still had a pet gray dragon
to run interference, but he died rather earlier than hoped, and
despite my best attempts to outrun them, Takahashi was completely
surrounded by air elementals about halfway across the level.  As her
wands of slow monster and hit points started to run out, I realized
she probably should have saved some full healing potions for this.
Fortunately, a ring of regeneration, a change of strategy (i.e., try
killing instead of outrunning), and some fortuitous engulfing by other
assorted vortexes got us both through it, and Takahashi got to the
portal in one piece.

But on the Plane of Water, Takahashi got the best present of all.
Just before she found the portal, Rodney summoned some nasties,
including a cockatrice, and I think this Astral Plane screen shot
neatly sums up the rest of the game:


